			HR-Nexus: Business Layer
Buisness layer created such that presentation layer does not requires data layer objects to access. From data layer, there are too much time need for fetching and searching data from files, so, here data structures are maintained on buisness layer which solve our problem for fast searching.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
No worry of memory for nearly 1 crore of records ?
Reason: If someone has 1 crore clients, then his revenue is too much and he can invest in bigger servers to maintain 1 crore+ records.
Let's suppose, one records contains 1000 bytes maximum: (address stores in records)
number_of_records=10000000		[1 crore]
one_record_size=1000 bytes
total_number_of_bytes=10000000 * 1000 =10000000000 bytes
total_number_of_kilo_bytes=	10000000000 / 1024  = 9765625 KB
total_number_of_mega_bytes= 	    9765625 / 1024  = 9537 MB
total_number_of_giga_bytes=            9537 / 1024  = 9.31 GB

Nearly 10 GB of Server Requires to store if one records is of 1000 bytes. 
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Buisness Layer is a layer in which we are creating functionalities for Presentation layer to use and manage data in a data structure for fast searching.
We are fetching data from Data Layer and populate in a data structure on starting of application, also add through using data layer add method, if successfully added then add in our data structure and similarly for all mehthods.
For getAll values, We are directly create a clone of one of our data structure and pass to presentation layer.
For managing multiple exceptions at the same time such that presentation layer works perfectly, we are creating BLException, Manage one generic exception + multiple property based (field_wise) exceptions.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

		DesignationManager
Over here, We are using singletone pattern method. In this method we are required to create such type of class in which only one object of that class is createdthrough complete cycle of the application. 
----------------------------------------------
How to implement Singletone Pattern?
1: Create Private Constructor of the Class[DesignationManager]
2: Create a static method for getClassObject[getDesignationManager() method]
3: Create a private static Pointer of Same class inside the class. 
Example: private static DesignationManagerInterface designationManager=null;
4: Create an object by allocating agaist that 'designationManager' static pointer and return it from getDesignationManager() method. Only create an object if there is null value against that static pointer. Otherwise return already alloted object address.
5: Create a private method of populateDataStructures() for retrieve data from Data Layer and populate in Data Structures that we have to create in Designation Manager.
----------------------------------------------
Data Structures: 
1: Map for Code Wise Data Management: 	
Example: Map<Integer,DesignationInterface> codeWiseDesignationMap
2: Map for Title wise data managerment in UpperCase String as title for inCaseSensitive Searching: 
Example: Map<String,DesignatonInterface> titleWiseDesignationMap
3: A Set for All data of designations that are collected in a set.
Example: Set<DesignationInterface> designationSet
(.......more added when required................)
----------------------------------------------
In class DesignationManager, We are named method as 'addDesignation()' instead of 'add()' only, Reason: In Manager class in business layer, it may possible that more than one entity are managed. So we have to configure at each place that for which it should be called. Over here, We are named it uniquly such that no more confusion/problem occured in future.
